Toolkit change for feat/input-mapping: PS3_INPUT_MAP, a controls file for
the host pad (keyboard, mouse buttons and wheel, controller buttons, mouse
camera settings).

A diff against the ps3recomp-fork/ working tree as of 2026-10-17 (fork
770660a + ps3recomp-fork-770660a-with-upstream-prs.patch + that day's
uncommitted work). Touches libs/input/cellPad.c, adds libs/input/pad_input_map.h
(the parser, header-only) and two standalone tests in libs/input/tests/, and
in libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.{m,h}: Shift/Control/Option reach the keyboard
pad, mouse buttons 4-8 get bits of their own, the wheel is counted, and the
capture setting comes from cellPad (so [mouse] in the file counts too).
With no file the layout is the old hard-coded one, side buttons included.

Apply from the repo root, rebuild, then fold it into
ps3recomp-fork-770660a-with-upstream-prs.patch as usual and delete this file:
    git -C ps3recomp-fork apply --check ../infamous2-lle/patches/pending/input-mapping.patch
    git -C ps3recomp-fork apply ../infamous2-lle/patches/pending/input-mapping.patch
Tests (from ps3recomp-fork/):
    cc -std=gnu17 libs/input/tests/test_pad_input_map.c -o /tmp/t1 && /tmp/t1
    cc -std=gnu17 -I include -isystem /opt/homebrew/include -isystem /opt/homebrew/include/SDL2 \
       libs/input/tests/test_pad_keymap.c -Wl,-dead_strip -o /tmp/t2 && /tmp/t2

